From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:36:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: leave a data-alignment fault to the SIGBUS path

The Mach exception server dispatches a fault as the guest's access
violation on the third identical (thread, pc, address) fault, to absorb
transient races. An unaligned atomic is declined, reaches the SIGBUS
path, and FEX completes it ("Handled unaligned atomic"); each pass
counts twice here. A loop that runs one atomic on one unaligned address
again hit the count on its second pass and got c0000005. Jurassic World
Evolution's DRM does that with xchg on unaligned stack slots:

  [unaligned-guest] REFUSED-OTHER insn=0xf8fb80db addr=0x702e01dcff ... keeping 80000002
  D 38 Handled unaligned atomic: new pc: 11DEDA268
  [mach-deliver] rev=ml369 #13 code=c0000005 pc=0x11deda264 ... addr=0x702e01dcff
  0038:err:seh:NtRaiseException Unhandled exception code c0000005 flags 0 addr 0x154eec10a

A data abort with the alignment-fault status (DFSC 0x21) is never an x86
access violation, so it is now always declined to the SIGBUS path.

Class: upstream-bug
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-09-jwe-commit-probe.md
Offered-upstream: no; the Mach exception server exists only in Madeira's iOS port
---
 build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
index 02e523e..2a411d6 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/signal_arm64_ios.c
@@ -7544,6 +7544,18 @@ static int ios_mach_deliver_guest_exception_inner( thread_t thread, arm_thread_s
           (pc >= 0x7000000000ULL && pc < 0x7400000000ULL)))
         return 0;
 
+    /* A data-alignment fault is never the guest's access violation (x86 has
+     * none): it is an unaligned atomic FEX emitted, and declining sends it to
+     * the SIGBUS path, where FEX completes it ("Handled unaligned atomic").
+     * The repeat count below cannot tell a loop that runs one atomic on one
+     * unaligned address again from a fault that repeats unserviced: its
+     * second pass dispatched c0000005 (Jurassic World Evolution's DRM, an
+     * xchg on an unaligned stack slot in a loop). */
+    if (exception == EXC_BAD_ACCESS &&
+        ((mc.__es.__esr >> 26) == ESR_ELx_EC_DABT_LOW || (mc.__es.__esr >> 26) == ESR_ELx_EC_DABT_CUR) &&
+        ESR_ELx_ISS_DFSC( (uint32_t)mc.__es.__esr ) == ESR_ELx_ISS_DFSC_ALIGN_FAULT)
+        return 0;
+
     /* transient-retry absorption: races with concurrent mprotect / FEX
      * invalidation are fixed by re-execution and were free retries under
      * the decline regime. Dispatch only on the 3rd identical
-- 
